    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Component B: % of investment budget spent</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2006-12-21" value="60%" year="2006">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2006-12-21"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2010-08-31"></period-end>
     <target value="80%">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The target value for this indicator is annual (incremental) based on the Fiscal Year of CMM that ends on December 31.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="89.9%">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">This value corresponds to 2010 (as this is an annual indicator, which reflects a value as of December 31). As of 2011, the valueofthe indicator is 29.6% (as of August 2011). The contracts for capital investments are progressing as planned, and it is expected(because most of the spending takes place at the end of the year) that by the end of 2011 the level of investment budget executedwillbe over the 80% target.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
